cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository in your research, please cite it."
title: "Trustworthy AI for Global Policy Evidence: Auditing LLM-Curated Digital-Nomad Visa Data and Evaluating Downstream Causal Consequences"
type: dataset
abstract: >
  Replication repository for a study of LLM-assisted curation and human
  verification of digital-nomad visa policy data, together with downstream
  macroeconomic and tourism analysis. The repository contains audited policy
  data, processed country-year data, analysis scripts, and generated figures
  used to evaluate how policy-data curation and treatment-date errors can
  propagate into comparative and staggered-adoption analysis.
keywords:
  - trustworthy AI
  - digital nomad visas
  - digital nomad visa
  - policy data
  - LLM
  - large language models
  - data auditing
  - human verification
  - causal inference
  - difference-in-differences
  - staggered adoption
  - TWFE
  - Callaway-Sant'Anna
  - policy research
  - replication
